From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: use the WSA interface for SM8650 WSA2 backends

The SM8650 AYANEO Pocket S2 and KONKR Pocket FIT topology declares the
speaker backend on the WSA2 codec DMA interface, but the ADSP firmware
those boards ship rejects WSA2 interface configuration. ROCKNIX's
SM8650 kernel rewrote the interface type to WSA inside its channel-map
workaround; the accepted upstream channel-map series that replaced it
keeps the mask handling but not the rewrite, leaving the speakers
silent. Restore the rewrite, scoped to SM8650 machines, on top of the
upstream mask computation.

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/apr.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/soc-dai.h>
@@ -747,6 +748,14 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < AR_PCM_MAX_NUM_CHANNEL; i++)
 		if (cfg->channel_map[i])
 			intf_cfg->cfg.active_channels_mask |= BIT(i);
+
+	/* The shipped SM8650 ADSP firmware rejects WSA2 (lpaif type 7)
+	 * interface configs; the mask above already selects the WSA2
+	 * slots. Remove when a fixed topology stops declaring type 7.
+	 */
+	if (intf_cfg->cfg.lpaif_type == 7 &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm8650"))
+		intf_cfg->cfg.lpaif_type = 2;
 
 	p += ic_sz;
 
